{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1464185-random-idea-for-sorcerer-major-template","id":1464185,"title":"Random idea for Sorcerer major template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-16T06:14:23-07:00","id":1464185,"title":"Random idea for Sorcerer major template","content":"So I have been obsessed with this passage from the Dark Eras companion for years now: &quot;There might once have been some form of greater sorcerer that conferred a true supernatural template, but those days are long passed from this world. Even if it was to be rediscovered this would not confer the kind of \u201cawakening\u201d seen elsewhere, since all sorcery stems not from some numinous higher world, but through living intersections between worldly Sekhem, chthonic powers, and Fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> I one day hope that we can get a greater sorcerer template, but until then I wanted to take a stab at making an idea for one.<br /> <br /> So rather than making a bunch of new systems and powers for this potential template, I thought at least for the abilities they can use I thought one could keep to the rule of three since it permeates ritual sorcery. A full template of these could potentially continue on with this:<br /> <br /> 1. Even greater mastery of Open Rites/Practical Occult. So that the full template sorcerers are even better at doing open rites than their normal counterparts. Maybe dip their toes into Ceremonies from Geist as well?<br /> <br /> 2. Keep Closed Rites as they are just that they can learn more than even the best mortal sorcerer<br /> <br /> 3. Utterances(with Utterances having three stages to them that makes sense to me) as their on the fly power<br /> <br /> Supernatural Tolerance/Power Attribute: Foundation instead of Sekhem, have them gather sekhem until it can be solidified into Foundation so unlike the Arisen they can't spend their trait and it starts at 1 and is bought up. They spend pillar points like mummies and can generate pillar points from their own soul.<br /> <br /> Edit: Here are some of my other thought doodling in this regard:<br /> <br /> The reason true sorcerers haven't been around en masse since Irem is because some of the Judges have actively tried to suppress it. The principle of keeping others from mastering the magic of Sekhem to the point they could be a threat since the only other notable source are their own slaves. <br /> <br /> &quot;Awakening&quot; for a ritual sorcerer is less of being able to see past the lie of the world like mages and more about driving a wedge of existential dread/fear of death into your soul that essentially cracks it so you can begin to let Sekhem flow into the cracks and fill them up. Which in turn lets you generate your own pillar points from your soul and spend them. <br /> <br /> Potential issues with the idea so far: Ritual slots are an issue so I am not sure how to replace/expand on that mechanic for steps 1-2, Second issue is figuring out if there should be more unique mechanics to develop here. So overall, I would like to get y'alls thoughts on this &lt;3 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","user":"Caedus","date":". 10-16-2021, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:03:53-07:00","id":1464200,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Reminds me a little of the idea I played out here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ll-minor-splat</a><br /> <br /> The intent there was much more to make mortal-ish sorcerers who can wield Utterances and Affinities in a manner similar to Arisen, but without the cycle of death and rebirth, but they interact with Pillar points (and therefore are very good at Rites) in a way similar to what you're describing. You're more than welcome to make use of whatever from Wrights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T17:11:43-07:00","id":1464234,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also the sidebar about taking Integrity loss to gain more Rite slots. I\u2019d combine these two sidebars/lores, and the Possessed from Inferno (1E), to make a sort of Infernalist template. Hey, the fiends of Duat might as well be the fiends of Hell, and \u201cspending Pillar points\u201d look a lot like chipping off bits of your soul for trading\u2026 This way we can look to 1E Vestments for ideas on Affinities and Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T09:41:35-07:00","id":1482259,"title":"","content":"I saw something in Geist the Sin-Eaters of Ceremonies just being more advanced open rites essentially, so I thought to continue on my idea here making Sorcerers proficient at Ceremonies and Rites(WTF) ones as well would make sense. Using the magic of our world after all as opposed to the supernal one to further differentiate them from Mages. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}